The Hydra render delegate this project builds upon lives in Cycles' own tree,
under src/hydra. The modifications this repository carries are distributed as
patches against that source (see patches/), not as a copy of it.

Some of those patches port work from Blender's own development, in which case
the patch message names the upstream pull request it comes from.

The MaterialX to Cycles translation owes its map to Ben Houston's work:

    blender-materialx-importer -- https://github.com/bhouston/blender-materialx-importer
    Copyright (c) 2026 Ben Houston
    Licensed under the MIT License

    The reference for which MaterialX nodes to translate to Cycles and how.
    Its list of supported node categories was the first checklist of the
    coverage work, before tools/mtlx_coverage.py measured against the whole
    MaterialX library. The translation in this project
    is written in C++ against the Hydra delegate's own mapping machinery.

